  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\nI. $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,i-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j$\n\nII. $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=x\\,i+2{e}^{y}\\,j$",
  "worked_solution": "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each vector field.\n\n- Vector field I doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II has a stream function. Indeed, the partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=1,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =2{e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=1+2{e}^{y}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
